>Hack is not a game to be won and put aside, it is a game to create
>great epic tales of woe, for without these the tales of glory would
>be hollow.

I agree with the above statement, although I don't have the time these
days to explore NH3.07 very much. My 5-year old son likes the game a lot, also,
although the level of playing is different ("Can I be the Knight? Please?")

THE SUGGESTION: I have been thinking about this a long time... With
reference to epic tales of Nethack games lost and won, would it be
possible to implement a semi-automatic log of play, e. g. after every
level the game would store the number of monsters killed/eaten/destroyed,
magic used, intrinsics gained, state of stomach after level, alignment
changes, temper of one's god etc... Then, afer the game, the log could
be retrieved from a file. The 'Semi' part would be an optional command
during the level - a line of text could be included in that level's log
(e.g. "Geez, was that nymph a tough one!")

What do others think? Epics of nethack would stay on hard-disk for
generations to come!

